When digitizing temporary records, agencies must meet the following standards:
Capture all information contained in the source records;
Include all the pages or parts from the source records;
Ensure the agency can use the digitized records for all the purposes the source records serve, including the ability to attest to transactions and activities;
Protect against unauthorized deletions, additions, or alterations to the digitized versions; and
Ensure the agency can locate, retrieve, access, and use the digitized versions for the records' entire retention period.
